Declare the arbitration probe before its first call

The probe defines nio_u_mark next to the matching watchdog (line ~3918) and
calls it from unlockForArbitration (line ~1946).  C++ wants the declaration
first, so the file stopped with three undeclared-identifier errors -- exactly
the failure that took the probe out of the series after run-342.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
index 5ea66c4..aca408e 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
@@ -88,6 +88,13 @@ enum{
 
 #define super IORegistryEntry
 
+/* nio: the arbitration probe writes straight to the framebuffer through the
+ * console blob's writer.  Its definition sits next to the matching watchdog
+ * further down the file, so the calls in unlockForArbitration need this
+ * declaration; without it the compiler stops with one "use of undeclared
+ * identifier" per call, which is what run-342 hit and left in the series. */
+static void nio_u_mark(const char *s);
+
 OSDefineMetaClassAndStructors(IOService, IORegistryEntry)
 
 OSDefineMetaClassAndStructors(_IOServiceNotifier, IONotifier)
